  "description": "A classic Thai stir-fry of pork belly and Chinese broccoli in oyster sauce, flavored with garlic and chiles.",
  "notes": "Notes: Crispy pork belly can be found in any Chinese grocery store or butcher that sells barbecue meat. Prepared crispy pork belly from different stores contains varying amounts of salt. Taste it before you proceed as you may find that you need less fish sauce than the amount called for in this recipe. When in doubt, it's best to add less fish sauce than you think prudent as you can always add more.",
